We need to implement main loop in the script.

We have current index.html with script placeholder replaced by config and state section. The script currently only includes config and state definitions, no code to get canvas context, no reset, no startLoop.

We need to add startLoop() function following spec, and also likely need a reset function and entry point (call reset). However task 3 focuses on adding startLoop function with cancelAnimationFrame handling, requestAnimationFrame loop, try/catch, and clear canvas each frame.

We can add it after the state section, maybe as // === LOOP ============================================================= section. We need to ensure no console errors.

Currently script doesn't have any reference to canvas context, so clearing canvas requires we have canvas and ctx defined somewhere. We may need to define them as part of loop. But the spec only asks for startLoop implementation; we might include canvas retrieval inside loop. Also we need variable loopId defined somewhere. Usually they add loopId global var.

We should add new code in script block after state. Possibly add other needed variables (canvas, ctx, lastTime, loopId). But the explicit requirement: add startLoop function with cancelAnimationFrame handling, requestAnimationFrame loop, try/catch, and clear canvas each frame.

Thus implement:

let canvas = document.getElementById('game');
let ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
let lastTime = performance.now();
let loopId = null;

function startLoop() {
  if (loopId !== null) cancelAnimationFrame(loopId);
  function tick(now) {
    try {
      const dt = Math.min((now - lastTime) / 1000, 0.1);
      lastTime = now;
      // clear
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
      // update & render could be called later (maybe stub)
    } catch (err) {
      console.error('loop error', err);
    }
    loopId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  }
  loopId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
}

Add at end call startLoop() maybe after definition. However tasks later may implement reset, update, render. For now call startLoop after define, so the page loads and no error.

We also need to ensure that canvas and ctx variables exist before startLoop is called, so they must be defined before startLoop.

Also need to use cancelAnimationFrame top of startLoop: we have handling.

Will also need to define loopId variable.

